ntrol.  \n- Playing the triple of 5s is strong in free play because it’s a mid-range triplet that can only be beaten by a higher triplet or bomb, forcing the landlord or teammate to respond.  \n- If the landlord passes, my teammate can take control; if the landlord uses a bomb early, that weakens their finishing power.  \n- Saving BlackJoker for later gives flexibility to beat a high single or rocket component.  \n- The triple_with_single options attach a weak card (♣4), but that exposes a low single unnecessarily. Pure triple is cleaner.  \n\n**Final choice:** Play the triplet to pressure opponents, conserve high cards, and signal strength to my teammate.  \n\n**Answer:** {"cards": ["♠5", "♣5", "♦5"]}'}
